{"name":"Laurel Garland","hex":"#68705c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"laurel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen shrub of species Laurus nobilis, having aromatic leaves of a lanceolate shape, with clusters of small, yellowish white flowers in their axils.","A crown of laurel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with laurel, especially with a laurel wreath.","To enwreathe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laurel"},{"term":"garland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A circular or linear decoration, especially one of plaited flowers or leaves, worn on the body or draped as a decoration.","An accolade or mark of honour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deck or ornament something with a garland.","To form something into a garland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garland","blocks":[{"text":"A garland is a decorative braid, knot or wreath of flowers, leaves, or other material. Garlands can be worn on the head or around the neck, hung on an inanimate object, or laid in a place of cultural or religious importance. In contemporary times, garlands are used to decorate, especially around holidays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Choinka.JPG/330px-Choinka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garland","wikidata":"Q756600"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/500px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/1280px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Daisy_chain.JPG/500px-Daisy_chain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm